From b6a4cf48cd70bba183a395fd159c3f7b9a357320 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dugs <dugahol@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:28:56 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 54/65] PCI: apple-h9p: read apple,msi-doorbell as a single
 cell

The binding defines apple,msi-doorbell as uint32, and the T8010 device
trees write it as one cell. The driver reads it with
of_property_read_u64(), which fails with -EOVERFLOW on a four-byte
property, so the driver has always used its built-in default. That
default happens to equal the T8010 value, which hid the mismatch.

Read the property as the binding defines it. The T8010 device trees
give 0xbffff000, the same as the default, so nothing changes there; a
SoC with a different doorbell can now describe it.

Ported from Orchard drivers/pci 0014.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
index ac8e06a5c..9c4660f24 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple-h9p.c
@@ -2006,6 +2006,7 @@ static int apple_h9p_pcie_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
 	struct pci_host_bridge *bridge;
 	struct apple_h9p_pcie *pcie;
+	u32 doorbell;
 	int ret;
 
 	bridge = devm_pci_alloc_host_bridge(dev, sizeof(*pcie));
@@ -2134,10 +2135,9 @@ static int apple_h9p_pcie_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		pcie->pwrctrl_powered = true;
 	}
 
-	ret = of_property_read_u64(dev->of_node, "apple,msi-doorbell",
-				   &pcie->msi_doorbell);
-	if (ret)
-		pcie->msi_doorbell = H9P_DEFAULT_MSI_DOORBELL;
+	pcie->msi_doorbell = H9P_DEFAULT_MSI_DOORBELL;
+	if (!of_property_read_u32(dev->of_node, "apple,msi-doorbell", &doorbell))
+		pcie->msi_doorbell = doorbell;
 
 	ret = apple_h9p_pcie_setup_msi(pcie);
 	if (ret)
